{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION to this ticket's own framing — two of my assumptions are REFUTED by the Phase 1 evidence\n\nI filed this ticket. The RCA comment above supersedes it on three points; recording the correction\nhere so the description is not read as current.\n\n**1. 'The gate does not scale to a 59-descendant epic' — REFUTED as the LLM driver.** The verifier\nmade only **5 `show_ticket` calls over 5 distinct tickets**; it never walked the 59 descendants.\n`graph=False` works as designed. Descendant count DOES drive ~88s of deterministic pre-LLM CPU\n(`child_closure_findings` 47.5s + `epic_bug_floor_findings` 41.0s), which contradicts\n`docs/llm-framework.md:680-683`, but that is not what exhausts the step budget.\n\n**2. 'Two exhaustions suggest non-convergence' — CONFIRMED, and upgraded from inference to\nmeasurement.** 264 tool calls; novelty 94-98% for calls 1-132, 12% for 133-198, **0% for 199-264**;\nloop entered at call #121 (50% of wall clock). A closed 4-call cycle repeated 31-37x against ONE file.\n\n**3. 'Raise the budget' — proven FUTILE, and my two attempts (480, then 1600) were wasted spend.**\nGenuine work needs ~118 distinct calls, so the existing 480 floor is already ~3.5x adequate. I\nescalated a budget when the correct read was that a budget was never the constraint.\n\n### The actual cause, and why it is much bigger than this epic\n\n`llm/pai_tools.py:99-140` — `search_files` returns `(no matches)` when `path` names a FILE, because\n`os.walk` on a file yields nothing and control falls through to the empty-result return. Measured in\none run: **48% of `search_files` calls passed a file path; 100% of those returned `(no matches)`;\n26 of 29 had the literal genuinely present.** `search_files('J1', …test_backend_characterization.py)`\nreturned `(no matches)` while `J1` sits on line 116.\n\n**This is a false-FAIL vector on a SIGNED gate**, not merely a loop: the completion-verifier prompt\ntells the agent `(no matches)` means the literal is absent, and encourages narrowing the path — which\nis precisely the call that lies. Any prior verdict that turned on a narrowed `search_files` is\nsuspect.\n\n### What stands from the original framing\n\nThe **trap** stands and is now better evidenced: `close_precheck.py:293-297` appends\n`Override with --force-close=\"…\"` unconditionally to what is a pure RESOURCE failure, while the\nbounded recovery that would have produced an honest verdict is unreachable (`LLMRunnerError` is a\nstrict ancestor of the caught types) and the computed diagnostic is dropped one frame from the\nsurface. So the gate offers the forbidden exit as its only reachable one, and simultaneously discards\nthe signal that would let anyone tune it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785929305041539001,"uuid":"95f2b69f-2102-4219-8e87-ff4f81d7a719"}